From 19f9f7b38daf22a701ba3350b2be33a5aad0fd67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:30:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: execution options of the material
 properties

Version 2 of the functions generated by the generic-parallel interface for
material properties: both functions take a last argument giving the
options of the execution (`mfront_gpmp_ExecutionOptions`, or null for the
default options), with the same meaning as for the behaviours:

- queue on which the computations are submitted: CUDA and HIP stream,
  SYCL queue (required), instance of the Kokkos execution space. The
  evaluation is ordered after the computations previously submitted to
  the queue. The queue of the SYCL backend was a specific argument of its
  functions: the signature no longer depends on the backend, and the
  mechanism of the specific arguments is removed;
- preservation of the stack size of the threads of the device.

The evaluation stays synchronous. Tests: stream which is not the default
one (CUDA, HIP), checked by a kernel writing the arguments on this stream
after a delay; instance of the execution space (Kokkos); missing SYCL
queue. Documentation of the strides of the arguments fixed (a null stride
denotes an uniform argument).
